    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lumbar plexus:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " forms w.in psoas major, in front of the lumbar transverse processes."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lumbar plexus branches:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " subcostal (T12), iliohypogastric (L1), ilioinguinal (L1), genitofemoral (L1, 2), lat femoral cutaneous (L2, 3), femoral (L2, 3, 4), obturator (L2, 3, 4), and the lumbosacral trunk (L4, 5), which joins the sacral plexus."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lumbar plexus supply:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " motor to the lower limb and pelvic girdle; sensory to the lower anterior abd wall, groin, upper thigh and pudenda."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral plexus:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " forms on the front of piriformis where the lumbosacral trunk (L4-5) joins the ventral rami of S1 to S4."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral branches b4 the divisions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " n. to piriformis (S1-S2), perforating cutaneous n. (S2-S3), posterior femoral cutaneous n. (S1-S3), pelvic splanchnic (parasympathetic) nerves (S2-S4), pudendal n. (S2-S4), perineal branch (S4)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral anterior division:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " n. to quadratus femoris and I. gemellus (L4-S1), n. to obturator internus and S. gemellus (L5-S2), and the tibial part of the sciatic n. (L4-S3)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sacral posterior division:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " S. gluteal n. (L4-S1), I. gluteal n. (L5-S2), and the common peroneal part of the sciatic n. (L4-S2)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Pudendal n.:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " from S2-4; the n. of the perineum and pelvic floor."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Pudendal n. course:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " leaves the pelvis thru the greater sciatic foramen below piriformis, turns around the sacrospinous ligament, passes thru the lesser sciatic foramen and runs in the pudendal canal on the obturator fascia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Pudendal n. branches:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " I. rectal n. (perianal skin and external anal sphincter), dorsal n. of the penis or clitoris, and perineal n. (superfic and deep perineal muscles and the external urethral sphincter)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
